    "md5": "cccf9982f67058bed901a09914cffd99",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1987,
    "chunk_text": "This confiscated land is kept in trust for illegal, armed Jewish settlers and for Jews around the globe, who might one day want to become citizens. Palestinians living in Israel cannot claim back land illegally taken from them, under the aegis of the Absentee Property Law of 1950. Most Sri Lankans are unaware of this background.\n\nThe Knesset (Israeli parliament) recently passed a law with compulsory death sentences to West Bank Palestinians who rise against their land being stolen and illegally settled. These events sear our moral consciousness like a white-hot iron and demand a desperate scream from the depths of the soul. Offering a glimmer of hope for the Global South, in its own discreet tenor, the International Court of Justice has issued such a cry of outrage, yet it seems to have fallen on deaf ears among the arbiters of the rules-based world order, whose agendas run contrary to justice.\n\nThe world witnessed regular instances of sheer inhumanity unfolding over just two decades, when the US-led alliances destroyed millions of poor lives in the Global South, of Afghanistan, Iraq, Libya, Somalia, Sudan, Syria and Yemen. So, why should I highlight Gaza as the major moral calamity of our time? Let me list five reasons why.\n\nPrimarily, the sheer brutality of the assault on a cornered, caged-in and defenceless population of women and children as a vastly disproportionate \u201cresponse\u201d to the retaliatory violence by the Palestinian Resistance.\n\nSecondly, the severity and indiscriminate nature of the devastation, laying waste to wholly unconnected structures, hospitals, churches, cemeteries and seats of learning falsely claiming they all harbour \u201cterrorists\u201d.\n\nThirdly, the speed at which this carnage was conducted, as if some undisclosed timeline exists for its \u201ccompletion\u201d. The use of an ever-changing rationale and pretexts, with claims such as enemy use of human shields or embedding among civilians, put forward at the aggressor\u2019s convenience."
