    "chunk_text": "More dates for Rajiv \u2026 in the UK\n\nRajiv Sebastian, veteran of Sri Lankan music and one of the island\u2019s most versatile entertainers, is back in the UK, as was reported in  The Island, last Tuesday (21), keeping his fans, in that part of the world, extremely happy and, literally, shouting for more!\n\nRajiv was originally scheduled to do four events but with his UK fans wanting more, two more dates have been added to the singer\u2019s itinerary.\n\nSaturday, 9th May, Rajiv will move into action at the Sri Lankan Cultural Day 2026, to be held at Southampton.\n\nThey say it\u2019s a full day event of family fun, with music, food and culture, including Avurudu games, etc., and I\u2019m sure Rajiv would love such a scene, and, of course, he will be there in a big way, with his Avurudu outfit of the sarama (sarong)!\n\nOn his return to Sri Lanka, Rajiv mentioned that he and his band The Clan have two overseas assignments lined up.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
