    "md5": "4f0ff5913b7f7da909f92c140a2e3a91",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1657,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s real estate leaders to chart  10-year vision at landmark RIUNIT Forum\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s property sector will come under the spotlight next month as the Research Intelligence Unit (RIUNIT) hosts a high-level forum titled \u2018Driving Growth Through Real Estate: 10 Year Plan\u2019, bringing together key stakeholders from across investment, policy, and urban development. Scheduled for 5 May from 2:30 p.m. at the Sales Gallery in Port City Colombo, the event aims to map out the sector\u2019s trajectory over the next decade, against the backdrop of evolving economic conditions and Sri Lanka\u2019s long-term urban ambitions.\n\nThe forum is the first in a series of planned sessions under RIUNIT\u2019s 10-year real estate roadmap \u2014and the agenda is as ambitious as the moment demands. Discussions will cover how Sri Lanka can claim a larger share of global real estate investment, how Port City can be positioned as a genuine investment magnet, and what a people-first approach to residential real estate might actually look like in practice.\n\n\u201cThis isn\u2019t just another industry conference,\u201d said RIUNIT Founder and CEO Roshan Madawela. \u201cWe want this to be the beginning of a structured, long-term plan that seeks to establish Sri Lanka as a leading international real estate investment destination that will attract a significant share of the\n\nestimated $ 1 trillion of institutional real estate investment in 2026\u201d. He added that \u201cthe conversation also needs to address the challenge of providing affordable housing for all as part of an integrated national strategy.\u201d\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake, has been invited as the Chief Guest."
  },
