    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s delegation, led by Rural Development, Social Security and Community Empowerment Minister Dr. Upali Pannilage also participated in several important side events. These included the event titled \u201cScience, Technology and Innovation in Bioeconomy for Sustainable Transformation: Advancing Strategies and Partnerships in the Asia-Pacific Region,\u201d organised by the People\u2019s Republic of Bangladesh, as well as the launch of the Technical Cooperation Highlights 2024\u20132025 publication. These engagements underscored the growing importance of innovation, technology transfer, and partnerships in achieving sustainable development outcomes.\n\nFurthermore, Sri Lanka expressed its support for the proposal by the People\u2019s Republic of China to host the 83rd Session of the Commission in Shanghai in 2027, recognising the importance of continued regional dialogue and cooperation.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s active participation throughout the Session reflects its steadfast commitment to multilateralism and to working collaboratively with regional partners to advance the 2030 Agenda. The successful conclusion of the 82nd Session reaffirms the critical role of ESCAP as a platform for fostering inclusive growth, strengthening resilience, and ensuring that no one is left behind in Asia and the Pacific."
